# The settings app, through the real keys (owner, 2026-09-17): what "controls"
# used to be was a list of letters somebody typed out, which had already drifted
# from the keys the game uses. This is the page that replaces it — sound, picture,
# the two holds a player may want as presses, and the keys read off the live input
# map, where they cannot drift again.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/settings.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
coast calm
wait 0.6

# --- from the pause page, where a player goes looking for it ----------------------
press pause
await app:pause 3
choose settings
press use
await app:settings 4
shot 01-the-settings-page with app:settings

# --- a level moved with the real keys ----------------------------------------------
choose sound.score
tap move_left
tap move_left
tap move_left
wait 0.3
shot 02-the-score-turned-down with app:settings

# --- a switch, and a hold made a press ---------------------------------------------
choose playing.crouch
tap move_right
wait 0.3
shot 03-crouch-as-a-press with app:settings

# --- the keys, read off the map itself ---------------------------------------------
choose keys
press use
wait 0.5
shot 04-what-each-key-does with app:settings

# --- and back out, one level at a time ---------------------------------------------
press pause
wait 0.4
press pause
wait 0.4
shot 05-back-to-the-world with land:coast
